            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Runic 2.18.1</h2>
<h3>Providers & Quotas</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Antigravity Gemini priority & multi-window quotas</strong>: Antigravity now leads with <code>Gemini 5h</code> and <code>Gemini Weekly</code> while preserving <code>Claude & GPT</code> 5-hour and weekly windows across provider cards, Overview, Reset schedules, widgets, exports, and <code>runic usage</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Consistent menu bar indicator</strong>: Menu bar percentages, wave bars, and Overview cards now follow the same active provider quota selection and ignore informational windows with no real denominator.</li>
<li><strong>Decoupled manual refresh & concurrency safety</strong>: Refreshing a single provider no longer stalls on or blocks other providers, bypasses URL caches, and coalesces concurrent per-account fetches with stale-write protection.</li>
<li><strong>Provider probe & parser hardening</strong>: Hardened 20+ provider fetchers and CLI probes — including <code>Antigravity</code> UTF-8 capture and timeouts, <code>Codex</code> RPC request timeouts and cancellation safety, <code>Claude</code> OAuth flat/scoped model deduplication and reset parsing, <code>Gemini</code> multi-PATH CLI resolution, <code>Muse Code</code> cancellation propagation, <code>MiniMax</code> and <code>Kimi</code> timestamp parsing, <code>Ollama Cloud</code> web-enrichment scoping, and prepaid balance alerts for balance-only providers.</li>
</ul>
<h3>CLI & Exports</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Reliable <code>runic usage</code> exit codes & full window output</strong>: <code>runic usage</code> now surfaces all additional model/quota windows consistently across text, JSON, CSV, and <code>runic reset</code>, honors <code>--provider all</code>, writes provider errors to <code>stderr</code> without corrupting stdout JSON, and exits non-zero when an explicitly requested provider fails.</li>
</ul>
<p><a href="https://github.com/sriinnu/Runic/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">View full changelog</a></p>
]]></description>
